WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:07.640
I'm Anna Sooväli.

2
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:10.320
I'll tell you about
this summer after school graduation

3
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.480
when the world went totally mad.

4
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:19.160
For starters,
I am a sad stuttering wuss

5
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.240
who wants to become
a furious and famous rapper.

6
00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:24.560
As in the Middle Ages I challenge you
to a duel and throw a glove

7
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.720
because here you see a woman
who is absolute best in her field.

8
00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:29.720
Man, you are getting on my nerves

9
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:32.600
because your bashful glance
won't rise higher from my breasts.

10
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.640
My...

11
00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:42.480
My lyrics are like concrete fists...

12
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:46.960
You are a... tablespoon.
Asshole...

13
00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.240
Shit!

14
00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:54.800
Sorry!
- Let me sleep!

15
00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.520
This is my family.
Yep. Here they are.

16
00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:03.320
Brother Jaan

17
00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.000
Father Martin

18
00:01:13.480 --> 00:01:14.560
Mother Monika

19
00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:15.720
Oh god...!

20
00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.560
Stop it!

21
00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.400
Grandfather Otto

22
00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.960
No bananas?

23
00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:30.600
I reserved these armchairs.
You promised to organize transportation.

24
00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.800
Martin, do you hear me?
- I got sacked today.

25
00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.880
WHY NOT?!

26
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.880
But let's go back in time
a couple of days

27
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:42.360
when the first signs
of this madness appeared.

28
00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:45.840
My older brother Gustav
left the university.

29
00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.600
Now he is lying in his room,
staring the ceiling.

30
00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:50.960
No one knows what's wrong with him.

31
00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:54.840
I think it's because of a woman.
An evil woman.

32
00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:57.120
Of course, it's so simple for men.

33
00:01:57.240 --> 00:02:01.520
I would give everything to blame some
bitch for my troubles, and not myself.

34
00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:08.200
Tu... tu... Tuna.

35
00:02:08.320 --> 00:02:14.080
In Tu... Tunguska
there is l... l... lots of...

36
00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.960
Lots of... Forests.

37
00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.760
And...

38
00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:29.080
N... n... natural resources.

39
00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:37.440
Oh, sorry. No need to stand up.
Sooväli, Prants and Atomic... Vadim.

40
00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:40.280
After class, my office.

41
00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:44.280
T... t... thanks a lot, T.. T... Tärnin.

42
00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:48.560
So...

43
00:02:52.040 --> 00:02:54.400
The school is about to end.

44
00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.520
Just bang! And it's over. Gone.

45
00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.200
But before that there is one more thing
to get over with, young people.

46
00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:02.000
The graduation ceremony.

47
00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:07.840
As the class teacher
I thought to give this task to you.

48
00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:13.440
I can't bother our athletes
with this matter.

49
00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.480
The last points need to be collected,
we must beat Nõmme school.

50
00:03:16.600 --> 00:03:18.000
I have the physics olympiad soon.

51
00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:20.680
Yes, Vadim,
but unfortunately this is not sport.

52
00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:24.440
This is almost...
anti-sport activity.

53
00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.320
So, put together a nice
and heartwarming program, alright?

54
00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:31.640
Well, you will have to...

55
00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:36.160
In life you have to to make right choices
and better choose things that suit you.

56
00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:40.760
There is no point to build a nest
in a tree if you can't fly.

57
00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:45.080
Great. Now, before the graduation exams
we have to organize a worldwide parade.

58
00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.200
I have no time for this.
I am too busy with my firm. Really.

59
00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.840
Listen, actually it's awesome!

60
00:03:52.960 --> 00:03:57.320
We can organize a party.
We could ask Carmen and others to help.

61
00:03:57.440 --> 00:04:00.800
This is a simple prom, Liis.
- And I have no time for this.

62
00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:03.400
We organize the party
and maybe they'll start talking to us.

63
00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:07.240
Liis, you will never be
Carmen's satellite. Accept it.

64
00:04:07.360 --> 00:04:10.360
You had 12 years for this, alright?
- Please, be rational.

65
00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:13.040
This is not about Carmen.
I could socialize with Keido.

66
00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:16.240
Please, Anna... Pretty please...!
- Jeez, Liis...

67
00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.880
Anna, in the name of our friendship.
Please?

68
00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:25.760
And I am standing like this.
Dan is on the stage.

69
00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:28.120
And I'm, like, throw this water!

70
00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:29.960
And then it comes flying,
like holy water.

71
00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.520
Holy water!
I didn't wash for three days.

72
00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:35.440
Sorry...
- What is going on here?

73
00:04:35.560 --> 00:04:38.800
So, Tärnin sent you
to the math olympiad?

74
00:04:38.920 --> 00:04:44.000
Well... Not exactly.
We will organize the prom and...

75
00:04:44.120 --> 00:04:45.600
What?

76
00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:48.560
Brats, no stepping on my shoes!

77
00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:53.920
We thought that maybe later
we could have a meeting in school

78
00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:56.200
and discuss it with you.

79
00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:01.640
And with Keido.

80
00:05:01.760 --> 00:05:04.760
You are really organizing the prom?

81
00:05:04.880 --> 00:05:06.760
Then we certainly
must hook up with you

82
00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:09.560
because otherwise
it would be a total disaster.

83
00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.040
Oh god, what are you doing!?
- You startled?

84
00:05:33.160 --> 00:05:35.680
Yes!
- Oh my god...

85
00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:39.960
This is from the Institute.
Grandma saved it from trash.

86
00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:42.760
It's name is Heino.
He likes to drink milk.

87
00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:45.000
Milk gives you strong bones.

88
00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:47.560
Hold Heino for a second.

89
00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:51.760
Don't you really have anything else
to do? Here, take your Heino.

90
00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:53.680
Yeah, I am useless and helpless,

91
00:05:53.800 --> 00:05:56.880
until grandma gets back
from the expedition.

92
00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.320
I don't know...
Go and wake my brother or...

93
00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:04.040
Or help my parents organize the jubilee.
- Jubilee? 50 is not a proper jubilee.

94
00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:07.200
Well, I don't know.
Go and play checkers in the park.

95
00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:12.240
Checkers is so close to checking out.
Checkers. For good...

96
00:06:12.360 --> 00:06:14.960
Johanna! Liis is here.

97
00:06:16.840 --> 00:06:20.000
Johanna? So posh...!

98
00:06:20.120 --> 00:06:22.560
Shut up.
- Hop, Johanna...!

99
00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:26.880
Anna, I was thinking...
When we go there in the evening,

100
00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:30.320
we cannot go like this.
Take a look at my clothes!

101
00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:33.920
Why not? What about your clothes?
- Anna, try to understand.

102
00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:38.920
We must dress up and not be like...
- Liis, stop it please.

103
00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:41.800
Anna, please!
Don't you understand?

104
00:06:41.920 --> 00:06:45.160
If you take us all down,
we'll be in the same mess.

105
00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:49.600
My dear, we'll be in a mess anyway.
We've been neighbors since birth.

106
00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:54.600
And this is the only mess.
- Anna... But if...

107
00:06:54.720 --> 00:06:58.360
Carmen will start taking me seriously
and Keido will notice me, at last.

108
00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:01.280
Stop it, Liis.
Just forget it, really.

109
00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.080
Anna, I am so close.
- Close to what?

110
00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:10.560
My dream!
Don't you get it? I'm so close.

111
00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.880
What kind of a dream is that?

112
00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:17.560
Some people still have dreams.

113
00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:31.880
You'll wear these shoes.
- I can't even walk with them.

114
00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:34.200
Then you'll learn! Step by step.

115
00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:37.040
Why do women need to have
these idiotic beauty standards?

116
00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:40.360
Men couldn't care less, really.
- Keido does care. Yes, he does!

117
00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:41.920
He is always dressed to kill.

118
00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:44.520
Dad's guests will be here soon.
Will you help me?

119
00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:46.600
I can't! I have this meeting in school.

120
00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:54.000
I'll just wear these shoes
around my neck, honestly. - Anna...

121
00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:18.360
Congratulations, Martin!

122
00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:37.320
All plastic...
- Stop this plonking.

123
00:08:37.440 --> 00:08:40.000
Vadim, you'll sit here
and take notes, alright?

124
00:08:40.120 --> 00:08:41.360
What do you mean?

125
00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:44.160
I need my hands to be free.
It would ruin the impression.

126
00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:46.680
Please stop plonking.

127
00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:51.680
Listen... Maybe it's weird
to have this lemonade jug like that?

128
00:08:51.800 --> 00:08:54.800
Yeah, obviously,
custard could be a killer, right?

129
00:08:54.920 --> 00:08:59.160
These shoes are really awful.
Please, can I take them off?

130
00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:01.880
Stand straight and you'll be alright.
- How?!

131
00:09:02.000 --> 00:09:04.000
No, stop it!

132
00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:11.480
Please don't do that.

133
00:09:14.680 --> 00:09:17.360
Goal! Go Brazil!

134
00:09:22.680 --> 00:09:24.720
Thank you, Monika.

135
00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:26.880
I see that you got
everything in order.

136
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:29.760
The man is the earner.
And the woman takes care of him.

137
00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:31.360
Come on, it's normal!

138
00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:34.280
The woman takes care of things
and the man makes the money.

139
00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:35.760
Really?
- Of course.

140
00:09:35.880 --> 00:09:39.040
I wouldn't mind
if the wife made big money

141
00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:42.200
and I would wear a gown
and help at home sometimes.

142
00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:45.280
My missus always
sets Martin as an example.

143
00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:47.760
"Martin does this, Martin does that...
Martin's got his own company."

144
00:09:47.880 --> 00:09:50.800
"Martin is the boss.
You, wimp, you are just a trucker."

145
00:09:50.920 --> 00:09:52.720
She just wants me to feel like shit!

146
00:09:52.840 --> 00:09:56.360
But let's be honest, it would be weird
for a woman to be a truck driver.

147
00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:58.120
No, you don't say that.

148
00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:01.400
Our firm hired this broad.

149
00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:07.040
Drives a truck like a pro!
Nothing wrong about it!

150
00:10:07.160 --> 00:10:08.800
No, alright, it is possible.

151
00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.040
Just the other day
I ordered a chimney sweeper.

152
00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:14.560
And it was a lady.
And she did a very good job.

153
00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:18.040
I even thought
of touching her button...

154
00:10:19.480 --> 00:10:22.680
Forget about this.
Metoo, you know!

155
00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:25.080
The sauna is ready, you rascals.

156
00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:50.880
Well...

157
00:10:55.560 --> 00:10:59.280
So, trucker.
Don't stand the heat anymore?

158
00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:01.880
Just 50 degrees and you already
go down on the lower bench!

159
00:11:02.000 --> 00:11:03.640
Better look at this!

160
00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:07.760
Once we were real bulls, right?

161
00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:09.880
Feeling so hot...

162
00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:13.520
I am still in great shape.
- Don't make me laugh...

163
00:11:13.640 --> 00:11:17.600
What? Laugh? Let's do some
arm wrestling and I'll show you!

164
00:11:17.720 --> 00:11:21.760
Did you hurt your arm?
I'll crush your noodles, my friend!

165
00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:25.320
What noodles, shit...!
- Peas on a line!

166
00:11:25.440 --> 00:11:27.400
Look here, boy...

167
00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:31.000
But guys, what about taking
a new picture? 30 years later?

168
00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:34.560
Stop it. No need for that...
- Come on! You don't look so fat!

169
00:11:34.680 --> 00:11:37.400
Who are you calling fat?!
- What...?

170
00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:41.200
Really, let's take a new picture.
- It's a great idea!

171
00:11:44.080 --> 00:11:48.880
Alright, you farts!
Get closer to each other!

172
00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:52.120
Pull in your stomach,
make some room for him!

173
00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:55.600
Show some muscle, you farts!

174
00:11:56.480 --> 00:11:59.600
Silence! Smile...

175
00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:06.360
Farts... So... One, two...
- Do it already!

176
00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:08.680
And three.

177
00:12:08.800 --> 00:12:11.000
Ott? What happened?

178
00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:23.880
What happened?
- Ott had a stroke.

179
00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:27.960
Why?
- They think they are still in their 20s.

180
00:13:06.680 --> 00:13:08.600
Cheer up, my dear.

181
00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:11.600
I am on the top of Mont Blanc.

182
00:13:11.720 --> 00:13:15.000
Our expedition had an unexpected turn.

183
00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:17.200
I am so bored without you.

184
00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:20.720
Do something, then.
Go get a job.

185
00:13:20.840 --> 00:13:23.040
Really?
- Of course!

186
00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:28.080
Do something useful.
Stop joking around at home.

187
00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:31.920
I miss you.
- I know, stupid.

188
00:13:43.200 --> 00:13:47.400
And the next morning we found out
why dad had been so lost in thought.

189
00:13:51.840 --> 00:13:53.480
What?

190
00:13:55.920 --> 00:13:57.880
What did you say, Martin?

191
00:14:01.840 --> 00:14:03.680
I got sacked.

192
00:14:05.360 --> 00:14:07.320
Sacked?

193
00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:12.480
But you are the boss. You sack others,
not the other way around.

194
00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:15.280
I sacked myself.

195
00:14:18.440 --> 00:14:20.760
Or... I quit.

196
00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:25.520
You wanted to quit
and you sacked yourself?

197
00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.400
I got enough.
I finally got enough.

198
00:14:38.600 --> 00:14:40.840
Yo, take a look.

199
00:14:40.960 --> 00:14:43.840
Yo, yo, take a look...

200
00:14:46.440 --> 00:14:49.200
Show it to all the gods.

201
00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:52.200
Yo, take a look.

202
00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:57.160
Yo, yo, take a look...

203
00:14:57.280 --> 00:14:59.800
Show it to all the gods.

204
00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:03.560
So, this is the thing.

205
00:15:03.680 --> 00:15:05.840
We need to pay the mortgage
and for the car lease.

206
00:15:05.960 --> 00:15:08.640
And the house bills.
Everyone must get a job.

207
00:15:08.760 --> 00:15:11.600
Jaan will go to the kindergarten.
- I could get a job as well.

208
00:15:11.720 --> 00:15:14.560
You don't worry.
- I am a strong man.

209
00:15:14.680 --> 00:15:17.840
Grandma also thought that I could
get a job. I'll get started.

210
00:15:17.960 --> 00:15:19.640
You are irresponsible, Martin!

211
00:15:19.760 --> 00:15:23.360
I didn't like this job for a long time.
Now it just clicked and...

212
00:15:23.480 --> 00:15:26.680
You were the manager in a big firm.
And you didn't like your job. Oh god!

213
00:15:26.800 --> 00:15:29.120
I was just choking there.
- Egoist!

214
00:15:29.240 --> 00:15:32.120
I was like a zombie.
- We already have one zombie in this house!

215
00:15:32.240 --> 00:15:35.560
Upstairs, eyes wide open.
- Zombie apocalypse...

216
00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:40.440
I am telling you. Everyone will
have to get a job! Or we'll be evicted.

217
00:15:44.880 --> 00:15:51.200
This is my first wise decision in 20 years.
- At least we are communicating again.

218
00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:54.880
You know, I want to have a job
that doesn't make me puke.

219
00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:59.560
You were a great climber as a kid.
- What's that got to do with it?

220
00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:04.720
Now when you are not a boss anymore,
it's useful to have physical skills.

221
00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:07.440
Anna, time to go to school!

222
00:16:19.840 --> 00:16:23.000
Liis, sorry. It was those shoes...
- Don't talk to me!

223
00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:25.880
And who will organize the prom?
- Normal people will do that.

224
00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:58.520
And there it was.
Like a revelation.

225
00:16:58.640 --> 00:17:02.320
Genka is looking for new talents.
A Rap contest, a record deal.

226
00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:06.720
I'll take part in the rap contest,
get the record deal and then you'll see.

227
00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:13.400
But yeah,
it's still a long way from the bottom.

228
00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:18.720
Yes?

229
00:17:18.840 --> 00:17:22.440
Anna, you'll go to the job interview
right after school. I'll send the address.

230
00:17:22.560 --> 00:17:24.640
A summer job before the university.

231
00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:27.680
Happy days are over.
Everything is over. Ok, bye.

232
00:17:27.800 --> 00:17:30.160
I'd like to see if anyone cares.

233
00:17:30.280 --> 00:17:32.480
If anyone cares if you have
your head in a plastic bag.

234
00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:34.560
Living on stolen purses.

235
00:17:34.680 --> 00:17:37.240
But your story, see,
doesn't mean shit to me.

236
00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:39.200
What are you, an idiot?

237
00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:41.960
Because I say so!

238
00:17:42.080 --> 00:17:44.360
Dodger Village tales.
All saints got together.

239
00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:46.600
These are Dodger Village tales.

240
00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:49.160
Dodger Village tales.
All saints got together.

241
00:17:49.280 --> 00:17:51.400
These are Dodger Village tales.

242
00:17:51.520 --> 00:17:53.560
Police van.

243
00:17:53.680 --> 00:17:55.400
Synthetic drug.

244
00:17:55.520 --> 00:17:56.880
Yes...

245
00:17:57.640 --> 00:18:00.960
And the salary is according to
the tryout period tariffs.

246
00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:03.880
And how long is the tryout?
- Three months.

247
00:18:05.160 --> 00:18:08.640
But I'll be here only for two months.
- Yes.

248
00:18:08.760 --> 00:18:10.400
And you must take into account

249
00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:14.320
that there will be
the adolescent worker reduction

250
00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:16.760
and the fact that you are
the weaker sex.

251
00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:20.760
But it's still a full time job.
And I am 18.

252
00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:26.440
I don't get it. Do you want this job
or did you come here to argue?

253
00:18:26.560 --> 00:18:28.280
Well...

254
00:18:28.400 --> 00:18:32.000
Your mom called and said that
you'd be a perfect dishwasher.

255
00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:35.120
If my mom thinks that way...

256
00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:38.960
Alright. These are the workplace rules
and the fire safety regulations.

257
00:18:39.080 --> 00:18:40.240
Read and memorize them.

258
00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:42.920
Rebecca!

259
00:18:43.920 --> 00:18:47.880
Rebecca will tell you about the work.
You'll start tomorrow, evening shift.

260
00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:51.240
See you then.
- Goodbye.

261
00:18:53.680 --> 00:18:56.640
Change you clothes here.
The locker on the right.

262
00:18:58.800 --> 00:19:00.880
Are you sure
that you want to work here?

263
00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:05.400
Don't you want to take your daddy's
money and have a soda by the pool?

264
00:19:06.680 --> 00:19:09.240
Actually my father got sacked
and I want to go to the university.

265
00:19:09.360 --> 00:19:12.240
Someone has to work in the summer.
- This is not a resort.

266
00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:16.280
If anyone fails, others have more work.
- I won't fail.

267
00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:21.520
Bugeye's talk was all bullshit.
- Who?

268
00:19:21.640 --> 00:19:26.480
Bugeye. The manager. There is no
such thing as an adolescent tariff.

269
00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:30.000
But how should I... - I don't know.
He is telling this to all youngsters.

270
00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:33.880
Think of something. We all work here
with some fucking tariffs...

271
00:19:34.000 --> 00:19:36.560
Ok, cool. Revolutions...

272
00:19:36.680 --> 00:19:38.880
Have you ever worked before?

273
00:19:39.000 --> 00:19:43.160
Well... Yeah.
At home I've done the washing up.

274
00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:46.160
Great. So it'll be the same scheme.
- What scheme?

275
00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:50.320
A week.
- What week?

276
00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:53.920
Karliito thinks
that you'll endure one week max.

277
00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:56.880
Karliito is one of the best
chefs in Estonia.

278
00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:02.200
Who called?

279
00:20:02.320 --> 00:20:05.760
Shit...!
Who is smoking here?

280
00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:45.240
One, me.
Two, also me.

281
00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:47.360
Blended like tobacco and pot.

282
00:20:47.480 --> 00:20:49.720
I am afraid of a stranger
on the bathroom wall.

283
00:20:49.840 --> 00:20:52.200
I lock the door
and leave him some bread.

284
00:20:52.320 --> 00:20:54.560
On a workday night
I wander in town.

285
00:20:54.680 --> 00:20:57.040
Naked breasts
in a Mustamäe apartment.

286
00:20:57.160 --> 00:20:59.280
Used for sniffing coke.

287
00:20:59.400 --> 00:21:01.760
Rihanna playing on YouTube.

288
00:21:01.880 --> 00:21:06.560
Everything will be alright,
sang the dead children in Norway.

289
00:21:06.680 --> 00:21:11.360
Metsakutsu. My Tallinn.
This life. My choice.

290
00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:13.760
Alcohol, G, two candies.

291
00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:16.160
Nasty, but this is life.

292
00:21:16.280 --> 00:21:18.560
Lower than gutter,
higher than my love.

293
00:21:18.680 --> 00:21:21.200
I live the life
that I owe to everyone.

294
00:21:21.320 --> 00:21:23.600
Matt face, bright clothes.

295
00:21:23.720 --> 00:21:25.840
Free bird on the outside,
the soul suffering inside.

296
00:21:25.960 --> 00:21:28.120
Life is easy, heart is heavy.

297
00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:30.840
Fuck off, you all,
let me go.

298
00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:38.560
I understood that you were
not coming back to work soon.

299
00:21:40.000 --> 00:21:41.480
The situation at home has changed

300
00:21:41.600 --> 00:21:44.080
and I'd like to come back from
the maternity leave at once.

301
00:21:47.560 --> 00:21:50.680
Don't worry about Jaan.
I'll find him a daycare and...

302
00:21:50.800 --> 00:21:52.320
So, you don't have to worry.

303
00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:56.320
We have all kinds of problems
with children anyway... Always.

304
00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:01.600
If it's possible,
I'd like to get my old job back.

305
00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:03.920
I was your best specialist here.

306
00:22:04.040 --> 00:22:06.520
Now Tõnu has this job.

307
00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:10.200
I know. Tõnu was my assistant.
I trained him myself.

308
00:22:10.320 --> 00:22:14.560
Yes, but...
We are counting on Tõnu at the moment.

309
00:22:14.680 --> 00:22:19.280
And we have
so many women with children.

310
00:22:19.400 --> 00:22:23.720
Permanent problems with illnesses...

311
00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:27.000
What position could I have,
potentially?

312
00:22:31.400 --> 00:22:34.560
I don't know...
Tõnu's assistant, maybe...

313
00:22:34.680 --> 00:22:36.840
Tõnu's assistant?!

314
00:22:39.840 --> 00:22:43.560
I don't have anything better
to offer you right now.

315
00:22:43.680 --> 00:22:47.440
They are looking for a new manager
and all that crap...

316
00:22:47.560 --> 00:22:51.320
Looking for a new manager?
- Yes. New owner, new requirement...

317
00:22:51.440 --> 00:22:53.320
Who else is applying for the job?

318
00:22:53.440 --> 00:22:57.240
There is no one except me.
It is just a formality.

319
00:22:58.120 --> 00:23:00.240
Yes? Hello.

320
00:23:00.920 --> 00:23:01.920
Exactly.

321
00:23:03.240 --> 00:23:09.960
And when would it be wise
to take over?

322
00:23:12.080 --> 00:23:13.600
Right.

323
00:23:15.960 --> 00:23:18.840
Yes, I've been thinking about it, but...

324
00:23:29.320 --> 00:23:31.640
I have no hope to get my job back.

325
00:23:31.760 --> 00:23:34.880
They are looking for a new manager?
- Yes, but it's a formality.

326
00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:38.200
Our manager just has to confirm
his position with the new owner.

327
00:23:39.120 --> 00:23:43.120
But you could qualify
as a manager yourself.

328
00:23:43.240 --> 00:23:48.440
Me? A woman with a small baby?
Competing this old fox? Forget it.

329
00:23:49.680 --> 00:23:52.200
But at least Anna got a job.

330
00:23:52.320 --> 00:23:54.600
And we need to wake up Kusti.

331
00:23:54.720 --> 00:23:56.600
And what about you, Martin?

332
00:23:56.720 --> 00:23:58.760
Everything is fine with me.

333
00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:01.760
Actually, I have an announcement.

334
00:24:03.360 --> 00:24:07.040
Look out, son,
not to get in trouble with the powers.

335
00:24:07.880 --> 00:24:11.920
I got my things in order.
I'm back in the saddle again.

336
00:24:12.040 --> 00:24:16.760
Yeah? You went back to work?
- No.

337
00:24:16.880 --> 00:24:21.640
But I know now what I'll be doing.
- Very nice.

338
00:24:24.400 --> 00:24:27.040
I'll be a fashion designer.

339
00:24:30.680 --> 00:24:34.160
Alright. Now it has happened.

340
00:24:34.280 --> 00:24:36.800
Monika...
I figured it all out.

341
00:24:40.600 --> 00:24:43.120
For my whole life
I wanted to be a tailor.

342
00:24:43.240 --> 00:24:45.160
Before I went to this business school.

343
00:24:45.280 --> 00:24:50.080
When I did bodybuilding
I made all my costumes myself.

344
00:24:50.200 --> 00:24:52.360
Bikinis and everything.

345
00:24:53.840 --> 00:24:56.040
I really liked to do that.

346
00:24:57.960 --> 00:25:01.440
I am a creative person.
Not an office supply.

347
00:25:01.560 --> 00:25:04.000
You have gone mad, Martin.
You are crazy!

348
00:25:08.400 --> 00:25:10.200
I'll be a model.

349
00:25:12.040 --> 00:25:14.320
I'll start training the catwalk.

350
00:25:15.280 --> 00:25:17.400
This is what I want to do.

351
00:25:31.640 --> 00:25:34.400
You will so pay for this!

352
00:25:39.320 --> 00:25:42.160
The bell strikes midnight.
The city is in flames.

353
00:25:42.640 --> 00:25:44.320
Yesterday is not your problem.

354
00:25:44.440 --> 00:25:46.640
Kiss the amulet,
raise the fist to the sky.

355
00:25:46.760 --> 00:25:49.160
I repeat,
yesterday doesn't bother me.

356
00:25:49.280 --> 00:25:52.400
The bell strikes midnight.
The city is in flames.

357
00:25:52.520 --> 00:25:54.240
Yesterday is not your problem.

358
00:25:54.360 --> 00:25:56.960
Kiss the amulet,
raise the fist to the sky.

359
00:25:57.080 --> 00:25:59.680
I repeat,
yesterday doesn't bother me.

360
00:26:06.560 --> 00:26:10.280
TALENT WAR

361
00:26:20.680 --> 00:26:23.120
I had nothing to lose anymore.

362
00:26:23.240 --> 00:26:26.760
And I was stupid enough to think
it couldn't get any worse.
